# ElderSafe Guardian — Project Rules

## Language

- Explain to the user in Traditional Chinese (Hong Kong) / 繁體中文（香港）.
- Write code comments in English only.

## Spec and progress

- Before making changes, read `PROJECT_SPEC.md` and `PROGRESS.md`.
- After completing the requested work, update `PROGRESS.md` to reflect what was done.

## Elder UI (`apps/elder`)

- Body text must be at least 20px.
- Primary buttons must be at least 72px tall.
- Colour contrast must meet WCAG AA.
- Do not hide important actions behind hover-only interactions; everything must work with tap / keyboard.

## Internationalisation

- All user-facing UI copy must come from next-intl message files (en / zh-HK).
- Do not hard-code interface strings in components or pages.

## Scope

- Only implement what the user asked for in the current request.
- Do not refactor unrelated code or change other pages “while you are there”.

## Secrets

- Never put API keys, tokens, passwords, or other secrets in source code.
- Use environment variables only (for example `.env.local`); do not commit real secrets.

## Handoff / testing

- When a feature is finished, give the user short, concrete manual test steps
  (how to start the app, which URL to open, and what to click / expect).
